Pin the Metal shading-language version instead of inheriting it from the host.

Rebase of ggml-metal-pin-msl-version.patch onto the ggml that llama.cpp v0.4.0
vendors, which routed both compile sites through
ggml_metal_compile_options_set_lang() and set languageVersion only on the tensor
branch. Off that branch it is still unset, so the original bug is unchanged:
Metal derives the MSL version from the SDK the *host process* linked against.
ggml is a library loaded into whichever binary the user runs, so shader
compilation depended on that binary rather than on the machine. Under
python.org's CPython 3.12 (linked against the macOS 12.1 SDK) the embedded
library fails to compile entirely --
"no matching constructor for initialization of 'threadgroup metal::half4x4[512]'"
-- and the Metal backend never initializes. Below MSL 3.1 the bf16 kernels are
additionally #undef'd by ggml-metal.metal while props.has_bfloat stays true.

Applied to all three ggml trees (ggml-*.patch). Only the trees on v0.4.0's ggml
take it -- llama.cpp itself, and stable-diffusion.cpp after _sync_ggml_abi()
copies llama.cpp's ggml over its own. whisper.cpp still vendors the older shape
and takes ggml-metal-pin-msl-version.patch instead; the two are mutually
exclusive, and the one that does not match is skipped as a no-op.

The ladder deliberately stops below MSL 4.0. That now overrides an upstream
default rather than making an unset one deterministic: v0.4.0 enables the tensor
API on M5/M6/A19/A20 and asks for MSL 4.0 to get its headers. Capping at 3.2
makes the tensor probe's dummy-kernel compile fail, so ggml_metal_device_init
clears props.has_tensor and the backend keeps the simdgroup kernels -- see
proposed/llama.cpp-metal-tensor-msl4.patch for why cyllama does not want the
tensor kernels enabled.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m
index e20a4e8..0d266b9 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m
@@ -28,7 +28,8 @@
 static const NSInteger MTLGPUFamilyMetal4_GGML = 5002;
 
 // MTLLanguageVersion4_0 is not present in older SDKs
-static const NSUInteger MTLLanguageVersion4_0_GGML = 4 << 16;
+// unused: ggml_metal_compile_options_set_lang() caps the ladder below 4.0
+static const NSUInteger MTLLanguageVersion4_0_GGML __attribute__((unused)) = 4 << 16;
 
 #if !GGML_METAL_EMBED_LIBRARY
 // Here to assist with NSBundle Path Hack
@@ -185,11 +186,44 @@ static void ggml_metal_library_build_index(ggml_metal_library_t lib) {
 
 // the tensor API headers are exposed to the shader compiler only at Metal language version 4.0
 static void ggml_metal_compile_options_set_lang(MTLCompileOptions * options, bool has_tensor) {
-    if (!has_tensor) {
-        return;
+    (void) has_tensor;
+
+    // Pin the version on every path instead of leaving it unset off the tensor
+    // branch. When languageVersion is unset, Metal derives the MSL version from
+    // the SDK the *host process* was linked against -- not from the running OS.
+    // ggml is a library loaded into whichever binary the user runs, so shader
+    // compilation followed the interpreter rather than the machine. Under
+    // python.org's CPython 3.12 (macOS 12.1 SDK) the library fails to compile
+    // outright:
+    //
+    //   error: no matching constructor for initialization of
+    //          'threadgroup metal::half4x4[512]'
+    //
+    // leaving ggml_metal_device_init with no library and no Metal backend.
+    // Below MSL 3.1 the bf16 kernels are also silently #undef'd (see
+    // ggml-metal.metal) while props.has_bfloat stays true.
+    //
+    // The ladder stops below MSL 4.0, so the Metal 4 tensor headers stay
+    // unavailable: the tensor probe in ggml_metal_device_init fails its
+    // dummy-kernel compile and clears props.has_tensor. That is the path the
+    // tensor API took before this branch existed; cyllama does not want the
+    // tensor matmul kernels enabled (see scripts/patches/README.md).
+
+    // spelled numerically so this still builds against SDKs predating the enum
+    // constants, matching the MTLLanguageVersion4_0_GGML precedent above
+    const NSUInteger msl_3_0 = (3 << 16) | 0;
+    const NSUInteger msl_3_1 = (3 << 16) | 1;
+    const NSUInteger msl_3_2 = (3 << 16) | 2;
+
+    if (@available(macOS 15.0, iOS 18.0, tvOS 18.0, *)) {
+        options.languageVersion = (MTLLanguageVersion) msl_3_2;
+    } else if (@available(macOS 14.0, iOS 17.0, tvOS 17.0, *)) {
+        options.languageVersion = (MTLLanguageVersion) msl_3_1;
+    } else if (@available(macOS 13.0, iOS 16.0, tvOS 16.0, *)) {
+        // MSL 3.1 does not exist here; 3.0 still compiles the library, but the
+        // bf16 kernels are compiled out -- an OS ceiling, not a choice.
+        options.languageVersion = (MTLLanguageVersion) msl_3_0;
     }
-
-    options.languageVersion = (MTLLanguageVersion) MTLLanguageVersion4_0_GGML;
 }
 
